# ⛔ LF EVERYWHERE, INCLUDING THE WORKING COPY.
# publish.js writes LF. Without this, Git checks these files out as CRLF on
# Windows, so the working copy no longer matches the bytes the publisher
# produces — and every republish shows 645 files as modified when nothing has
# actually changed. That noise is how a real change gets missed in a diff.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
